{
  "decline_reason": "",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "You can seek an extension even after the acceptance deadline has expired; an extension is not automatic.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMA1995/s224",
          "quote": "(4) The time allowed for doing a relevant act may be extended, whether before or after that time has expired."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "legislation"
    },
    {
      "text": "For a missed acceptance deadline, the Manual directs you to apply under section 224 and regulation 21.25, even if you are still within the six-month “easy” extension period.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part16/1/1/4",
          "quote": "Therefore, if an application for an extension of time is made after the time has expired, even if it is within its six month \"easy\" extension period, it will still have to be made under the provisions of section 224(4) and regulation 21.25."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "Lodge the late extension request with the appropriate fee and a declaration explaining both why you need more time and why you did not request the extension before the deadline.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part16/1/1/4",
          "quote": "These provide that a late application for an extension of time must be accompanied by a declaration setting out both the grounds for needing an extension of time, and also the reasons the application for the extension was not filed in time (together with the appropriate fee)."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "Under section 224(2), the Registrar may grant an extension where an error or omission by you or your agent, or circumstances beyond your control, caused the relevant act not to be done in time.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMA1995/s224",
          "quote": "(2) If, because of: (a) an error or omission by the person concerned or by his or her agent; or (b) circumstances beyond the control of the person concerned; a relevant act that is required by this Act to be done within a certain time is not, or cannot be, done within that time, the Registrar may, on application made by the person concerned in accordance with the regulations, extend the time for doing the act."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "legislation"
    },
    {
      "text": "Section 224(3) also permits an extension where the Registrar considers that special circumstances justify it.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMA1995/s224",
          "quote": "(3) If: (a) a relevant act that a person is required by this Act to do within a certain time is not, or cannot be, done within that time; and (b) on application made by that person in accordance with the regulations, the Registrar is of the opinion that special circumstances exist that justify an extension of that time; the Registrar may extend the time for doing the act."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "legislation"
    },
    {
      "text": "If relying on your or your agent’s error or omission, the Manual says your submissions need to establish a genuine error or omission that caused the need for extra time.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part15/4/4/1",
          "quote": "Any submissions regarding an extension sought on this ground would need to satisfy the Registrar that the need for the extra time was caused by a genuine error or omission on the part of the person concerned, or his or her agent."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Manual cautions that merely having forgotten to act is unlikely to justify an extension.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part15/4/4/1",
          "quote": "Given the impact that the extension sought might have on other parties, the Registrar would be unlikely to grant the extension because someone merely \"forgot\" to carry out an action."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "An application under section 224(2) or (3) for an extension of more than three months must be published and may be opposed as prescribed.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMA1995/s224",
          "quote": "(5) If an application is made under subsection (2) or (3) for an extension of time for more than 3 months, the Registrar must publish the application in accordance with the regulations."
        },
        {
          "ref": "TMA1995/s224",
          "quote": "(6) A person may, as prescribed, oppose the granting of the application."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "legislation"
    },
    {
      "text": "If the application has already lapsed and you also want deferment, the Manual requires the extension of time for acceptance to be approved before the deferment request can be processed.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part17/1#1",
          "quote": "If a trade mark application has lapsed prior to acceptance, an extension of time for acceptance will need to be filed. This extension will need to be approved before a deferment request can be processed."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "The supplied passages do not specify the fee amount or filing channel, and do not reproduce regulation 21.25, so they are not a complete filing checklist.",
      "quotes": [],
      "authority": "none"
    }
  ],
  "declined": false,
  "concepts_used": [
    "GC-0093",
    "GC-0097",
    "GC-0116",
    "GC-0046",
    "GC-0040",
    "GC-0098",
    "GC-0096"
  ]
}
